How C works in your character's head (they are sure of it and nobody has corrected them):
Two assignments happen at the same time

The quiz shows:
int a[3] = {5, 6, 7};
a[0] = a[1];
a[1] = a[2];
a[2] = a[0];

What is a now?
Options: "{6, 7, 6}" or "{6, 7, 5}"

Your character picks "{6, 7, 5}", because of how C works in their head. Then type what they would type in the "Why?" box:
one message, at most 30 words, the way this character really types. No lecture, no rule names.

